Vridhi — Nuisance Models Development and Evaluation
Hepsiba — DML Integration and Treatment Effect Estimation
WEEK 3: Model Development and Integration
Objective: Integrate the team's modules, develop the nuisance models, and obtain an initial Double Machine Learning (DML) treatment effect estimate.

1. Jaswanth — Feature Engineering and Pipeline Validation
Day 1: Review the Existing Pipeline
Review feature_engineering.py, feature_preprocessing.py, feature_split.py, and feature_pipeline.py.
Verify that the required dataset columns are available.
Review the current X (confounders), T (treatment), and Y (outcome) configuration.
Keep the existing pipeline unchanged until the team confirms the final variable definitions.
Deliverable: docs/week3_feature_review.md

Day 2: Update Feature Configuration
After the team confirms the final variables:

Configure the treatment, outcome, and confounder columns.
Add validation for missing or incorrectly named columns.
Check for duplicate or overlapping variables.
Ensure that the selected variables match the team's DML configuration.
Deliverable: Updated src/feature_engineering.py

Day 3: Validate Feature Preprocessing
Handle missing values appropriately.
Encode categorical variables such as Education and Marital_Status.
Ensure preprocessing is fitted on training data and applied consistently to test data.
Check for data leakage between training and testing datasets.
Deliverable: Updated src/feature_preprocessing.py

Day 4: Implement Consistent Train-Test Splitting
Split X, T, and Y using the same row indices.
Validate the shapes of all training and testing outputs.
Use a fixed random seed for reproducibility.
Check treatment distribution in the training and testing datasets.
Deliverable: Updated src/feature_split.py

Day 5: Integrate the Feature Pipeline
Connect dataset loading, preprocessing, and splitting modules.
Execute the complete pipeline.
Validate the resulting feature columns and data shapes.
