Mid review aaj hai to kaam ko chhota rakhte hain. Handbook ke hisaab se Week 1 + Week 2 check hota hai, aur tumhare hisse ke liye ye 5 cheezein taiyaar rakho.

## 1. Pehle 5 minute: GitHub check
Review mein 14 din ke andar team ke 10 alag din ke commits dekhe jaate hain, aur har active member ke commits uski apni branch mein hone chahiye. Repo mein jaake ye chalao:
```bash
cd OneDrive\Documents\GitHub\EconoCausal-Dynamic-Pricing
```
```bash
git fetch origin
```
```bash
git log origin/vridhi-gautam --since="14 days ago" --format=%ad --date=short
```
Jitni alag dates aayein (ek hi date baar baar aaye to ek hi gino), unhe gino. Teeno doosri branches (`origin/jaswanth`, `origin/sekhar`, `origin/hepsiba`) ke liye bhi yahi chalao. Team ke total alag din 10 ya usse zyada hone chahiye. Kam hon to review se pehle mentor ko batao, aur chupao mat.

## 2. Review mein kya dikhana hai (tumhara hissa)
| Kya | Kaise dikhao |
|---|---|
| Week 1: React dashboard | Dashboard chalao (jo bhi command tum use karti ho, `npm start` ya `npm run dev`), upload page aur budget input dikhao |
| Week 2: nuisance models | `python src/nuisance_models.py` chalao, AUC table dikhao |
| Week 3 ka ab tak ka kaam | `python src/nuisance_predictions.py`, `Reproducible: True` dikhao |
| Docs | `docs/model_selection.md`, `docs/week3_nuisance_model_plan.md` |
| Work Distribution Document | PDF jo maine banaya tha. Handbook ke hisaab se ye Month 1 ke Mid Review se pehle submit hona tha. |

## 3. Viva ke liye short jawab (apne shabdon mein bolna)
- **Nuisance model kya hai?** Do models: ek treatment ka (kisko campaign dikhaya gaya, propensity score), ek outcome ka (kisne response diya). Dono confounders se predict karte hain, taaki DML in confounders ka asar hata sake.
- **Cross-fitting kyun?** Har customer ki prediction aise model se aati hai jo us customer par train nahi hua. Isse overfitting se residuals bias nahi hote.
- **Kaunsa model chuna aur kyun?** Random Forest, dono ke liye. Outcome AUC 0.778 aur treatment AUC 0.726, dono log loss mein bhi sabse behtar. Logistic regression baseline thi aur tree models usse behtar nikle.
- **Purchase columns kyun hataye?** `total_purchase_amount` aur `total_purchases` shayad campaign ke baad ke hain (post-treatment). Unhe confounder banane se bias aa sakta hai, isliye timing confirm hone tak hataye hain. Sensitivity check bhi kiya: DML estimate 0.2361 (saath mein) aur 0.2725 (bina).
- **Overlap check?** Propensity score 0.013 se 0.79 ke beech hai, koi 0 ya 1 ke paas nahi. Lagbhag 5% customers 0.05 se neeche hain.
- **Leakage kaise roka?** `check_config()` har run par check karta hai ki `Response` aur `AcceptedCmp1-5` features mein na aayein. `Response` aur `campaign_response` identical hain.

## 4. Limitations jo khud batani hain
- Treatment, outcome aur confounder roles abhi team ne final confirm nahi kiye.
- Purchase columns ka timing unconfirmed hai.
- Estimate abhi validated causal effect nahi hai (refutation tests baaki hain).
- LightGBM nahi try kiya.
- Mock/simplified dataset hai, to results real-world ke liye nahi hain.

## 5. Ek honest baat
Jo bhi code Claude Code ya mujhse bana hai, uske sawal tumse honge. Review se pehle `src/nuisance_models.py` ek baar padh lo, khaaskar `oof_predict` aur `dml_residuals`.

Mid review ka social media video aur attendance bhi marks mein hain (5-5 marks), to wo bhi na bhoolna.

Review ke baad bata dena kaisa gaya, aur kya feedback mila. Uske hisaab se Day 5 (evaluation script) aur baaki Week 3 karenge. Abhi koi cheez atak rahi ho to bolo.

