## 3. Aaj raat tak ye karo
**Week 1 aur Week 2 ke write-ups abhi submit karo.** MID tab par lock ka nishan hai, to wahan jaake dekho ki mid review ke liye bhi write-ups chahiye ya nahi. Write-ups ek-ek short update hote hain ("What did you build this week?"). Ye drafts hain, jo maine tumhare asli kaam se likhe hain. Apne shabdon mein thoda badal lena:

**Week 1 write-up**
> Set up the React (Vite) dashboard for EconoCausal with a sidebar layout, a CSV upload interface (parsed with PapaParse, with a data preview) and a marketing budget input. Agreed dataset columns and repository structure with the team. Blocker: none major; the upload validation initially used a proposed schema that later had to be matched to the real dataset.

**Week 2 write-up**
> Built the nuisance models for Double ML in `src/nuisance_models.py`: outcome model (campaign_response) and treatment model (campaign_exposure), comparing Logistic Regression, Random Forest and Gradient Boosting with 5-fold cross-fitted predictions. Random Forest was best (outcome AUC 0.778, treatment AUC 0.726). Added a leakage guard, a propensity overlap check, a sensitivity run without the purchase columns, and documented everything in `docs/model_selection.md`. Open issue: the timing of the purchase columns is still unconfirmed with the team.

**Week 3 write-up**
> Wrote the Week 3 nuisance model plan and split the code into `treatment_model.py` (cross-fitted propensity scores with validation and an overlap summary) and `outcome_model.py` (cross-fitted outcome predictions). Added `nuisance_predictions.py`, which combines both into one aligned table of propensity, outcome predictions and DML residuals, with alignment checks and a reproducibility test. Saved outputs in `results/`. Next: precision/recall evaluation and the final results document.

