## Step 3: Viva ki taiyari

Viva mein tumhare apne kaam ke sawal aate hain. Ye 8 sawal sabse zyada probable hain. Jawab apne shabdon mein bolna, ratta mat lagana.

**1. Tumne project mein kya kiya?**
> Maine Double ML ke nuisance models banaye: ek treatment model jo predict karta hai ki kise campaign dikhaya gaya (propensity score), aur ek outcome model jo predict karta hai ki kisne response diya. Saath mein React dashboard banaya jisme CSV upload aur budget input hai.

**2. Nuisance model kya hota hai, aur DML mein kyun chahiye?**
> DML mein hum confounders (age, income, etc.) ka asar treatment aur outcome dono se hatana chahte hain. Isliye pehle confounders se T aur Y ko alag-alag predict karte hain. Jo bacha (residual) wo confounders se saaf hai, aur usse treatment effect nikalte hain.

**3. Cross-fitting kyun?**
> Agar model usi data par predict kare jis par train hua hai to overfitting hoti hai aur residuals bias ho jaate hain. Cross-fitting mein har customer ki prediction aise model se aati hai jo us customer par train nahi hua (5-fold).

**4. Kaunsa model chuna aur kyun?**
> Random Forest, dono ke liye. Outcome AUC 0.778 aur treatment AUC 0.726, aur log loss bhi sabse kam. Logistic Regression baseline thi, aur tree models usse behtar nikle.

**5. Purchase columns kyun hataye?**
> `total_purchase_amount` aur `total_purchases` shayad campaign ke baad ke hain (post-treatment). Unhe confounder banane se bias aa sakta hai. Timing confirm hone tak hataye. Sensitivity check bhi kiya: DML estimate 0.2361 (saath mein) aur 0.2725 (bina).

**6. Overlap check kya hai?**
> Propensity scores 0 ya 1 ke paas nahi hone chahiye, warna kuch customers ke liye treated aur untreated comparison nahi ho paata. Mere scores 0.013 se 0.79 ke beech hain, aur lagbhag 5% customers 0.05 se neeche hain, jo ek limitation hai.

**7. Leakage kaise roka?**
> `check_config()` har run par check karta hai ki `Response` aur `AcceptedCmp1-5` features mein na aayein. `Response` aur `campaign_response` identical hain, to Response ko feature banate to leakage hota.

**8. Dashboard ke baare mein bata.**
> React (Vite) app hai. Sidebar, CSV upload (PapaParse se parse hota hai, preview dikhta hai), required columns ka validation (real dataset ke columns par), aur budget input. Uplift curves aur prescription Week 3-4 ka kaam hai.

## Limitations khud batana (isse achha impression padta hai)
- Treatment, outcome aur confounder roles team ne abhi final confirm nahi kiye.
- Estimate abhi validated causal effect nahi hai (refutation tests baaki hain).
- Mock/simplified dataset hai.
- LightGBM nahi try kiya.

## Agar kuch na pata ho
Seedha bolo: "Ye mujhe abhi pakka nahi pata, main check karke batati hoon." Galat jawab dene se behtar hai.

## Practice
Ek baar `src/nuisance_models.py` kholkar `oof_predict` aur `dml_residuals` ko apne shabdon mein bol ke samjhao. Chaho to main inpe 3-4 sawal poochh sakti hoon aur tum jawab likho.

Practice karni hai ya review ke liye taiyar ho? "practice" likh do to main ek-ek sawal poochhungi.

