Claude Code VS Code mein hai to wo viva ki taiyari ke liye bahut kaam ka hai. Files kholne ke liye bas ye kaafi hai, Claude ki zaroorat nahi:

## Files kholne ka sabse tez tareeka
VS Code mein repo folder khula ho (**File > Open Folder** se `EconoCausal-Dynamic-Pricing`), phir **Ctrl + P** dabao aur file ka naam type karo (jaise `nuisance_models`), Enter dabao. Ek ek karke ye 7 kholo: `nuisance_models.py`, `nuisance_predictions.py`, `treatment_model.py`, `outcome_model.py`, `model_selection.md`, `week3_nuisance_model_plan.md` aur `App.jsx`.

## Claude Code ko viva ke liye use karo
Claude panel mein ye prompts do (ek-ek karke). Isse wo code ko tumhare liye explain karega, aur kuch change nahi karega:

```
Explain src/nuisance_models.py line by line in simple English, as if
preparing me for a viva. Focus on oof_predict, dml_residuals and
check_config. Do not edit any files and do not run git commands.
```

```
Ask me 5 viva questions about my nuisance models (cross-fitting, why
Random Forest, overlap check, leakage, purchase columns). Ask one at a
time and wait for my answer before giving feedback.
```

```
Explain frontend/src/App.jsx: how the CSV upload, PapaParse and the
required-columns validation work. Do not edit any files.
```

## Dhyan rakho
1. Prompt mein "do not edit files" likhna zaroori hai, taaki review se pehle code na badle.
2. Git commands khud chalana, Claude Code se commit ya push mat karwana.
3. Jo bhi wo samjhaye, apne shabdon mein ek baar bolke dekho. Viva mein tum samjhaogi, Claude nahi.

Ab Claude Code se explain karwao, aur jo samajh na aaye wo mujhse puchh lo. Chaho to main yahi pe "practice" mode mein sawal poochhu, bata do.

