Kuch toot nahi hai. Order ulta ho gaya: `git add` chala jab PDF `docs` folder mein thi hi nahi, isliye "did not match any files" aaya, aur commit mein kuch gaya hi nahi. Abhi chal raha `git push` bhi bas "Everything up-to-date" bolega, kyunki bhejne ko kuch hai nahi.

## Fix, ek ek karke

**1.** Pehle push ko khatam hone do (ya Ctrl + C dabao agar atka rahe).

**2.** `results/nuisance_predictions.csv` "modified" dikha raha hai kyunki review ke liye script dobara chalayi thi. Us file ko commit karne ki zaroorat nahi, to purani state par wapas kar do:
```bash
git restore results/nuisance_predictions.csv
```

**3.** PDF ko `docs` folder mein copy karo. Download wali PDF aksar `Downloads` folder mein hoti hai:
```bash
copy "%USERPROFILE%\Downloads\EconoCausal_Work_Distribution_Document_v2.pdf" docs\Work_Distribution_Document.pdf
```
`1 file(s) copied` aana chahiye. Agar "cannot find the file" aaye, to dekho ki PDF ka asli naam kya hai:
```bash
dir "%USERPROFILE%\Downloads\EconoCausal*"
```
(Naam mein `(1)` jaisa kuch ho sakta hai. Jo naam dikhe wahi copy command mein daalna.)

**4.** Check karo ki file `docs` mein aa gayi:
```bash
dir docs
```

**5.** Ab commit karo:
```bash
git add docs/Work_Distribution_Document.pdf
git commit -m "Add Work Distribution Document (Weeks 1-3)"
git push
```

`data/` ko `git add` mat karna, wo Untracked hi rahega.

Ek aur chhoti baat: pichhli `code ...` wali command ke end mein `App.jsxv` likha dikh raha hai, shayad typing mein extra `v` aa gaya. Isse `App.jsx` VS Code mein na khula ho, to VS Code mein **Ctrl + P** se `App.jsx` kholo.

Commit ka screenshot bhej do. Phir demo aur viva practice par chalte hain.

